{"seconds": 78.0, "exit": 0, "final": "Perfect! After 1.Nf8+ Kh8 2.Ne6+, we have the same position where the Black queen is under attack. So the main forcing line is:\n\n**1.Nf8+** \n- If 1...Kg8, then 2.Ne6+ and all moves lose the queen\n- If 1...Kh8, then 2.Ne6+ and Black loses the queen\n\nThis is a textbook knight fork! The knight checks the king and attacks the queen simultaneously, winning Black's most powerful piece.\n\n**Coaching note (approx 75 words):**\n\nWhen you have a powerful knight and opponent's king on the back rank, look for forcing knight checks that also attack undefended pieces. Here, Nf8+ forces the Black king to move while the follow-up Ne6+ creates a fork\u2014the knight checks the king AND attacks the undefended queen on d4. Black cannot save both, so White wins the queen, which is decisive. Train yourself to spot these patterns: knight checks on h-files often create forks.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Nf8+\", \"line\": [\"Nf8+\", \"Kg8\", \"Ne6+\", \"Kh7\", \"Nxd4\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "1Q6/p2N2pk/1pp2p1p/8/P2qn3/7P/6PK/8 w - - 2 39"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "1Q6/p2N2pk/1pp2p1p/8/P2qn3/7P/6PK/8 w - - 2 39"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "1Q6/p2N2pk/1pp2p1p/8/P2qn3/7P/6PK/8 w - - 2 39"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "1Q6/p2N2pk/1pp2p1p/8/P2qn3/7P/6PK/8 w - - 2 39", "move": "Nf8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "1Q6/p2N2pk/1pp2p1p/8/P2qn3/7P/6PK/8 w - - 2 39", "move": "Qh8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "1Q6/p2N2pk/1pp2p1p/8/P2qn3/7P/6PK/8 w - - 2 39", "move": "Qg8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "1Q3N2/p5pk/1pp2p1p/8/P2qn3/7P/6PK/8 b - - 3 39", "move": "Kh8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "1Q3N2/p5pk/1pp2p1p/8/P2qn3/7P/6PK/8 b - - 3 39", "move": "Kg8"}}, {